  'SASSA grants: which ones exist and who qualifies',
  'If someone in your house is 60 or older, is caring for a child under 18, or cannot work because of a disability, SASSA may owe them a monthly grant and most people who qualify never ask. From April 2026 the old age grant is reported as R2,400 a month (R2,420 from age 75) and the child support grant as R580 per child, but those figures come from news reports, so confirm them at the SASSA office or on sassa.gov.za before you count on them. Every grant has a means test: SASSA looks at your income and, for the older person''s grant, what you own. Applying is free and nobody may charge you to help.',
