  ARRAY['sars', 'tax', 'tax return', 'tax refund', 'refund from sars', 'do i need to file', 'tax threshold', 'efiling', 'auto assessment', 'auto-assessment', 'irp5', 'itr12', 'filing season', 'tax season', 'mobiapp', 'sars app', 'paye', 'my employer deducts tax', 'medical aid tax', 'tax number', 'register for tax']::text[],
  'Do you need to file with SARS, and is a refund waiting',
  'If you earn under the tax threshold you pay no income tax, and if your employer deducted PAYE anyway, or you paid medical aid or retirement contributions, a refund may be sitting at SARS. The threshold for the year to 28 February 2026 was R95,750 for people under 65; third-party tax sites report R99,000 for the year that started 1 March 2026, so confirm on sars.gov.za. Filing season for the 2026 year ran from July to 23 October 2026, with auto-assessments issued in early July: if SARS auto-assessed you and it is right, you do nothing and the refund is paid; if it is wrong, you file the return on eFiling or the SARS MobiApp.',
  'you earned a salary with PAYE deducted, paid medical aid or retirement fund contributions, or got an auto-assessment SMS',
  'your only income is a social grant or cash piece jobs under the threshold and no tax was ever deducted; there is nothing to refund',
  ARRAY['Check your IRP5 from your employer for the ''PAYE'' line: if tax was deducted and your yearly income is near or under R95,750 (year to 28 February 2026), a refund is likely', 'Register on sars.gov.za for eFiling or download the SARS MobiApp with your ID and tax number; if you have no tax number, the registration creates one', 'If SARS sent an auto-assessment, open it in the app and check the income and deductions against your IRP5 and medical aid certificate; if correct, you do nothing and any refund is paid into the bank account SARS has for you', 'If it is wrong or you were not auto-assessed, file the ITR12 return in the app before the filing deadline SARS publishes each year (23 October 2026 for the 2026 season)', 'Make sure the bank account on your SARS profile is in your own name; refunds are only paid to a verified account', 'Never pay a ''tax refund agent'' who messages you on WhatsApp; SARS does not use agents like that, and its contact centre is 0800 00 7277']::text[],
  'free to file; the tax threshold was R95,750 for under-65s for the year to 28 February 2026 and is reported as R99,000 for the 2026/27 year by third-party sites, confirm on sars.gov.za (checked 2026-10-30)',
  'medium',
  '2026-10-30'::date
)
